<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Active Directory — FreeITSM</title><style>body{font:15px system-ui;max-width:1000px;margin:32px auto;padding:16px;color:#223;background:#f5f7fa}section{background:white;padding:24px;margin:20px 0;border-radius:8px}label{display:block;margin:12px 0}input:not([type=checkbox]),select,textarea{display:block;padding:8px;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%}textarea{font-family:monospace;min-height:170px}button{padding:10px;margin:5px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#result{position:sticky;top:0;background:#eef;padding:12px}</style></head><body><h1>Active Directory</h1><p><a href="../">System</a> · <a href="../../ad-sign-in.php">Corporate sign-in</a></p><p>Single-domain sign-in is sufficient. Multi-domain sign-in and AD-managed permissions are independent opt-ins. Keep a separate local emergency administrator.</p><pre id="result" role="status"></pre>
<section><h2>Deployment settings</h2><form id="settings">
<label><input type="checkbox" name="enabled"> Enable native AD authentication</label><label><input type="checkbox" name="multi_domain"> Enable multi-domain authentication</label>
<label>Default authentication provider<select name="default_provider_id"></select></label><label>Authorization domain (optional)<select name="authority_provider_id"></select></label>
<p>Without an authorization domain, existing FreeITSM permissions apply. New users start in self-service. Turning AD authorization off removes AD-managed grants while retaining independent assignments.</p>
<label>Protected local administrator ID<input name="emergency_analyst_id" type="number" min="1" value="1" required></label>
<label>Refresh interval (seconds, 60–3600)<input name="refresh_seconds" type="number" min="60" max="3600" value="900"></label><label>Maximum password attempts per login (1–2)<input name="max_attempts" type="number" min="1" max="2" value="1"></label>
<label>Allowed registration email domains (comma separated)<input name="allowed_email_domains" placeholder="company.example"></label><label>Public deployment URL (HTTPS, including deployment path)<input name="public_url" type="url" placeholder="https://itsm.company.example"></label><label>Existing outbound SMTP mailbox ID<input name="smtp_mailbox_id" type="number" min="1"></label><label>Verification expiry (minutes, 15–30)<input name="verification_minutes" type="number" min="15" max="30" value="20"></label><button>Save settings</button></form></section>
<section><h2>Directory providers</h2><p>Create a provider before enabling AD authentication. Blank service password preserves the stored encrypted credential.</p><select id="editProvider"><option value="">New provider</option></select><form id="provider"><input name="id" type="hidden"><label>Name<input name="display_name" required maxlength="100"></label><label>Priority (lower first)<input name="sort_order" type="number" value="0"></label><label><input name="enabled" type="checkbox" checked> Enabled</label><label><input name="authentication_enabled" type="checkbox" checked> Allow authentication</label><label><input name="trusted_linking" type="checkbox"> Trust for automatic cross-domain linking</label><label>Read-only service account password<input name="bind_password" type="password" autocomplete="new-password"></label><label>Directory connection and search settings (JSON)<textarea name="config" required></textarea></label><p>Use mounted CA files and TLS. Service searches require a read-only bind identity; no Domain Admin privileges are needed.</p><button>Save provider</button></form></section>
<section><h2>Group mappings</h2><p>Map security-group objectGUIDs to existing access groups. Highest priority wins; ties combine module grants. Configure modules in existing access groups before granting analyst access. Empty groups grant no analyst permissions.</p><form id="mapping"><label>Provider<select name="provider_id"></select></label><label>Group GUID (32 lowercase raw hex characters)<input name="group_guid" pattern="[a-fA-F0-9]{32}" required></label><label>Access group<select name="access_group_id"></select></label><label>Priority (higher wins)<input name="priority" type="number" value="0"></label><label><input name="remove" type="checkbox"> Remove this mapping</label><button>Save mapping</button></form><pre id="mappings"></pre></section>
<section><h2>User authorization and identity review</h2><label>Employee profile<select id="profiles"><option value="">Select profile</option></select></label><button id="diagnose">Inspect authorization, linked identities and history</button><button id="refresh">Force-refresh selected profile</button><pre id="diagnostics"></pre>
<h3>Test directory lookup</h3><form id="lookup"><label>Provider<select name="provider_id"></select></label><label>Corporate email<input name="email" type="email" required></label><button>Test lookup</button></form>
<h3>Reconcile an existing employee</h3><p>Verify the employee's identity before linking. Existing user IDs and history are preserved. The protected emergency administrator cannot be linked. Use the raw GUID returned by Test lookup.</p><form id="link"><label>Existing employee user ID<input name="user_id" type="number" min="1" required></label><label>Existing analyst ID (optional)<input name="analyst_id" type="number" min="1"></label><label>Provider<select name="provider_id"></select></label><label>Verified objectGUID<input name="guid" pattern="[a-fA-F0-9]{32}" required></label><label>Previous GUID (required only to approve replacement of a linked account)<input name="previous_guid" pattern="[a-fA-F0-9]{32}"></label><button>Approve identity link</button></form></section>
<script>
const csrf=<?=json_encode(adCsrf(),JSON_HEX_TAG)?>,url='../../api/ad/admin.php';let state;
const defaults={host:'dc1.corp.example',secondary_host:'',port:636,transport:'ldaps',timeout:5,ca_file:'',user_base:'DC=corp,DC=example',group_base:'DC=corp,DC=example',bind_dn:'svc-freeitsm@corp.example',email_attribute:'mail',name_attribute:'displayName',nested_groups:true};
function options(el,rows,blank){el.replaceChildren();if(blank)el.add(new Option(blank,''));for(const r of rows)el.add(new Option(r.name||r.display_name||r.email,r.id));}
function populate(form,data){for(const el of form.elements){if(!el.name)continue;if(el.type==='checkbox')el.checked=Number(data[el.name])===1||data[el.name]===true;else if(el.name in data)el.value=data[el.name]??'';}}
async function load(){const r=await fetch(url);state=await r.json();if(!state.success)throw Error(state.error);const cfg={...state.config,allowed_email_domains:JSON.parse(state.config.allowed_email_domains).join(', ')};
for(const el of document.querySelectorAll('select[name=provider_id],select[name=default_provider_id],select[name=authority_provider_id]'))options(el,state.providers,el.name==='authority_provider_id'?'None — use FreeITSM permissions':'Select provider');
options(document.getElementById('editProvider'),state.providers,'New provider');options(document.querySelector('#mapping [name=access_group_id]'),state.groups);options(document.getElementById('profiles'),state.profiles,'Select profile');populate(document.getElementById('settings'),cfg);document.getElementById('mappings').textContent=JSON.stringify(state.mappings,null,2);}
async function send(data){const r=await fetch(url,{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json','X-CSRF-Token':csrf},body:JSON.stringify(data)});const j=await r.json();document.getElementById('result').textContent=j.success?'Saved / completed':j.error;if(!j.success)throw Error(j.error);return j;}
for(const [id,action] of [['settings','config'],['provider','provider'],['mapping','mapping'],['link','link'],['lookup','lookup']])document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('submit',async e=>{e.preventDefault();try{const d=Object.fromEntries(new FormData(e.target));for(const el of e.target.querySelectorAll('[type=checkbox]'))d[el.name]=el.checked;if(id==='settings')d.allowed_email_domains=d.allowed_email_domains.split(',').map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);if(id==='provider')d.config=JSON.parse(d.config);const j=await send({...d,action});if(id==='lookup')document.getElementById('diagnostics').textContent=JSON.stringify(j.identity,null,2);else await load();if(id==='provider')e.target.bind_password.value='';}catch(e){document.getElementById('result').textContent=e.message;}});
document.querySelector('#provider [name=config]').value=JSON.stringify(defaults,null,2);
document.getElementById('editProvider').onchange=e=>{const p=state.providers.find(p=>String(p.id)===e.target.value);const f=document.getElementById('provider');f.reset();populate(f,p||{id:'',config:defaults});f.config.value=JSON.stringify(p?.config||defaults,null,2);f.bind_password.value='';};
document.getElementById('diagnose').onclick=async()=>{try{const r=await fetch(url+'?profile_id='+encodeURIComponent(document.getElementById('profiles').value));const j=await r.json();document.getElementById('diagnostics').textContent=JSON.stringify(j.profile||j,null,2);}catch{document.getElementById('result').textContent='Diagnostics unavailable';}};
document.getElementById('refresh').onclick=async()=>{try{await send({action:'refresh',profile_id:document.getElementById('profiles').value});document.getElementById('diagnose').click();}catch{}};
load().catch(e=>document.getElementById('result').textContent=e.message);
</script></body></html>
